honest question though ... 

```js
document.body.innerHTML = '<!marker>';
const { nodeType, data } = document.body.childNodes[0];

nodeType === Node.COMMENT_NODE;
data === 'marker';
```

will it be, at least, an `instanceof` something that **extends** `Comment` ? ... or how doesn't this break the Web for anyone that accidentally had a `<!--marker-->` in the layout? 🤔

