> will it be, at least, an `instanceof` something that **extends** `Comment` ? ... or how doesn't this break the Web for anyone that accidentally had a `<!--marker-->` in the layout? 🤔

We prefer not to do this as it would force us to make those nodes have a mutable `CharacterData`.
But we'll analyze for web compat to see if subclassing `Comment` is something we absolutely have to do.
Another web compat issue is creating a new nodeType, which hasn't been done in over a decade.
This is all being actively considered, and we'll fall back to "a comment subclass" instead of "a new node type" if the web compat reasons are strong enough.

If we use a subclass of `ProcessingInstruction` with the `name` set to the first part of the `data` up to any whitespace, and support pseudo-attributes, the interface could be something like this (supporting the same attribute-related methods as `Element` but without `Attr` nodes, without NS methods, and no `TrustedType` support):

```
interface Marker : ProcessingInstruction {
  attribute DOMString name;
  sequence<DOMString> getAttributeNames();
  undefined setAttribute(DOMString name, DOMString value);
  undefined removeAttribute(DOMString name);
  boolean toggleAttribute(DOMString name, optional boolean force);
  boolean hasAttribute(DOMString name);
};
```

Maybe we can leave out pseudo-attributes for now though.

The HTML parser can trim a trailing `?` so that polyglot is still possible.

